## CZD Purple — live + installable image for Charleston Zero Day
##
## Built through Kali's live-build-config as variant "czd" (build.sh copies this tree in).
## This is stock Kali Purple with KDE Plasma, plus the eight czd-* packages that arrive as
## local .debs in packages.chroot. Nothing of Kali's is removed or renamed.

## Live images always want these
kali-linux-core
kali-desktop-live

## Desktop — Plasma 6, the only desktop CZD ships
kali-desktop-kde

## Kali Purple: the defensive menu and theme packages that make Kali "Purple"
kali-menu-purple
kali-themes-purple

## Kali Purple tool menus (Identify / Protect / Detect / Respond / Recover)
kali-tools-identify
kali-tools-protect
kali-tools-detect
kali-tools-respond
kali-tools-recover

## Kali's default toolset stays, so the 01–13 menu is intact under ALL APPS
kali-linux-default

## Installer — Calamares from the live session (batch 08). debian-installer stays reachable
## from the boot menu's advanced submenu; Calamares is what "Install CZD Purple" launches.
calamares
calamares-settings-debian

## Toolkit reach (batch 07): Kvantum for non-KDE Qt, Plex Mono from Debian, Archivo from czd-purple-tokens
qt6-style-kvantum
fonts-ibm-plex

## CZD defensive tooling — menu 14 and up (respin edit 06). Add what the SOC track actually uses.
#<package>
